            "Even today, hunters and travelers who respect the tradition leave offerings before entering the forest. A bit of tobacco or cachaça, placed on a tree trunk, would be enough to please Curupira. That way, he would let the visitor go on their way in peace. This practice still exists in many riverside communities of the Amazon.",
