            "On festa junina nights, when the riverside bonfire fairs along the Amazon rivers light up, the air fills with woodsmoke, the sound of accordion players, and an old mystery no one dares name aloud. It is on nights like these, the elders say, that the river draws near the land almost indiscreetly, as though it wished to join the festivities.",
            "It was on one such occasion that a stranger appeared, from no one knew where, in an impeccable white suit and a wide-brimmed hat, always shod in fine boots that no one ever saw stained with mud. Courteous, elegant, and soft-spoken, the young man quickly won over anyone who caught his eye, though no one could say his name or which family he belonged to.",
